Report truncation when max_db_limit caps a list

Carries upstream change 1001033, patch set 1 (commit
fad88d3be22ee61abf7de9e74aba52003bbaa164, Change-Id
Ib116c537a9bef959b28e577fe55c194471c8aa40), proposed on master on
2026-08-16 and not merged. No keystone tag contains it. The diff is
carried unchanged: the same added and removed lines in the same four
files, cut against this tag with patches 0001 to 0005 applied.

list_users and list_groups in keystone/identity/backends/sql.py and
list_projects in keystone/resource/backends/sql.py page through
sqlalchemyutils.paginate_query with hints.get_limit_or_max();
list_projects_acting_as_domain calls list_projects, so /v3/domains
takes the same path. Hints.get_limit_or_max in
keystone/common/driver_hints.py returns CONF.max_db_limit when no
limit was requested, and build_driver_hints in
keystone/server/flask/common.py sets hints.limit only when the request
carries limit or list_limit applies. Each driver sets
hints.limit["truncated"] only inside "if hints.limit:", and
wrap_collection adds truncated and the next link only when hints.limit
says the list was cut. An unpaged GET /v3/users, /v3/groups,
/v3/projects or /v3/domains therefore answers at most max_db_limit
(default 1000) entries as if the list were whole: no truncated key,
and links.next is null. On 2026-11-21 in the C5C3/playground cluster
(keystone 29.0.0, default max_db_limit) GET /v3/users returned 1,000
of 3,260 users and GET /v3/projects 1,000 of 1,923 projects that way
(C5C3/cobaltcore#1842). Upstream tracks it as Launchpad bugs 2134607
and 2163597.

The drivers now read the effective limit once, pass it to
paginate_query and call hints.set_limit(limit, truncated=True) when
the page holds that many rows, so a cut list carries truncated: true
and a links.next with marker and limit. A client that follows
links.next reads the whole collection in pages of max_db_limit rows,
one bounded query per page: 4 requests for the playground's 3,260
users. gophercloud's pagers do that (UserPage.NextPageURL returns
links.next). A client that sends one GET and does not follow
links.next still receives one page. A list of exactly max_db_limit
rows is reported as cut and its next page is empty, because the
driver compares with >=, as it already does for a requested limit.
Callers inside Keystone that pass no hints get the same rows as
before. exception.MarkerNotFound for an unknown marker is raised
before the changed lines, and the patch keeps it. A client that
follows links.next sends the id of the previous page's last entity
as marker, and the drivers look that row up before the query. When
another request deletes that entity between two pages, the next page
answers 404 MarkerNotFound. gophercloud's Pager.AllPages then returns
the error without the pages it read, and the caller lists again from
the start. Before the patch an unpaged list answered one page with a
null next link and could not meet this race; a request that sets
limit meets it upstream as well. Continuing after a deleted marker
would drop upstream's refusal of an unknown marker, so the diff keeps
change 1001033 as it is. An error of the query itself, such as
oslo.db's DBConnectionError, reaches the caller before
hints.set_limit runs, and patch 0003 answers it with 503 as before.
The patch needs no operator configuration: the keystone-operator
renders neither max_db_limit nor list_limit.

The patch keeps upstream's release note,
releasenotes/notes/report-truncation-with-max-db-limit-89d415e6d6be36cd.yaml,
so that it reverse-applies as a whole once a tag contains the change,
which is how check-image-patches.sh --apply recognises a patch to
retire.

Tests: no existing upstream test moves. The patch adds
test_list_no_limit_capped_by_max_db_limit and
test_list_no_limit_below_max_db_limit to PaginationTestCaseBase in
keystone/tests/unit/test_v3.py, which DomainPaginationTestCase,
ProjectPaginationTestCase, UserPaginationTestCase and
GroupPaginationTestCase in keystone/tests/unit/test_v3_resource.py
run: six resources under max_db_limit = 4 answer four entries with
truncated true and a next link with the fourth entry's id as marker
and limit=4, and under max_db_limit = 100 the answer has no truncated
key and a null next link. With only the test hunk applied,
test_list_no_limit_capped_by_max_db_limit fails in all four classes
on 29.0.0 and on 30.0.0.

Proof: test_list_truncation_patch_applied in
tests/container-images/verify_keystone.sh drives list_users,
list_groups and list_projects of the built image against an in-memory
SQLite database with max_db_limit = 3.

keystone/identity/backends/sql.py, keystone/resource/backends/sql.py
and keystone/tests/unit/test_v3.py are the same in keystone 29.0.0
and 30.0.0, and the twins under patches/keystone/2026.1/ and
patches/keystone/2026.2/ differ only in their Applies-to line.

Applies to keystone 30.0.0 (2026.2).

Upstream status: proposed as https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/keystone/+/1001033.

